    "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the current ages of Alex and Allison based on the information given. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Determine Diane's age when she turns 30:**\n   Diane is currently 16 years old. When she turns 30, she will be 30 years old.\n\n2. **Determine Alex's age when Diane turns 30:**\n   According to the problem, when Diane turns 30, she will be half the age of Alex. Therefore, Alex's age when Diane turns 30 will be:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 30 = 60\n   \\]\n   So, Alex will be 60 years old when Diane turns 30.\n\n3. **Determine Allison's age when Diane turns 30:**\n   According to the problem, when Diane turns 30, she will be twice as old as Allison. Therefore, Allison's age when Diane turns 30 will be:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{30}{2} = 15\n   \\]\n   So, Allison will be 15 years old when Diane turns 30.\n\n4. **Determine the current ages of Alex and Allison:**\n   Since Diane will be 30 years old in 4 years, Alex will be 60 - 4 = 56 years old now, and Allison will be 15 - 4 = 11 years old now.\n\n5. **Calculate the sum of the ages of Alex and Allison:**\n   The sum of the ages of Alex and Allison now is:\n   \\[\n   56 + 11 = 67\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the ages of Alex and Allison now is \\(\\boxed{67}\\).",
